1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,764
The Report Said Mountain. They Chose Oil.

2
00:00:04,764 --> 00:00:31,160
Before dawn on March 8 the Israeli Air Force bombed Iran’s oil facilities for the first time in the war. Four people were killed. Black smoke from the storage tanks spread over the capital. The sun came up and it did not get light. There were fears of fuel shortages, of poisoned water and soil, of damage to people’s lungs. The war’s targets were moving from military sites to the country’s livelihood.

3
00:00:31,760 --> 00:01:01,708
Dr. Leila Shirazi looked from one screen to the other. On the left, Tehran. Black smoke cut across the city. On the edge of the band sat the Evin district, where her aunt lived. Nine days without a phone line. On the right, Fordow. The signal held at yesterday’s level. Sam Farrell brought two coffees. “Word from the liaison office. Tel Aviv asked about your Fordow report. Raw data and all.”

4
00:01:02,308 --> 00:01:30,720
“But look at that. They didn’t hit the mountain. They hit the oil.” Instead of breaking what could not be broken, they chose to choke the country’s breath. The grammar of the war had changed overnight. The report spoke of a mountain, and the decision chose oil. “It’s a choice.” Leila zoomed all the way in on Evin. The satellite would not show her roses. Target lists name buildings, never the people downwind.

5
00:01:31,320 --> 00:02:00,452
Before dawn on March 9, Capt. Marcus Webb watched from the bridge as the map grew. Ten days ago only two countries had been colored in. Now the color had spread. Lebanon, Iraq, Kuwait, Bahrain, Qatar, the Emirates, Saudi Arabia, Jordan, Oman. The sea off Cyprus, the skies over Turkey. Twenty-five years in the Navy, and no manual covered a war that spread this far in ten days.

6
00:02:01,052 --> 00:02:28,144
Sarah Callahan’s place was empty. Before she left she gave him a page torn from her notebook. The Bahrain bureau’s number, and one line below it. The days your hands are quiet scare me most. He kept it in his breast pocket. Marine insurance had jumped sixfold in a week. On a map a war spreads as color. At sea it comes as distance. The distance at which you cannot help.

7
00:02:28,744 --> 00:02:32,484
Epic Fury continues in Episode 5.
